If you mean that social systems are a result of human action and not human
design, we're struggling (as usual) with a mere semantic difference.
The point is, what should conscious human actors palced in such a complex
system do?

>Communism was put down in a previous post (or two...;-)...but it works
>wonderfully for ants. All quantities are known..._all_ work for the good
>of the whole...

Ant colonies are complex systems. Nests and other cooperative behavior are
emergent properties. All quantities may be know to you as a human observer,
but any specific ant has only local, partial knowledge.

>[. . .]the system may
>work for a while, but falls apart due to chaos theory sooner or later...

